text:
maria: FYI escalated from @support — customer seeing schema validation failures because tool_call.arguments arrive truncated in the stream. they pasted what we got on our side:

[LOG] RECEIVED SSE CHUNK: data: {"tool_call": {"name": "charge", "arguments": "{\"amount\":100,\"currency\":\"USD\",\"metadata\":\"user-123""

maria: and then it just stops, parser throws JSONDecodeError: Unterminated string starting at: line 1 column 85

ryan: request id? model? region?

maria: req=rq_9fH3k, model=redwood-llm-inference-2024, region=us-west-2. customer is behind a managed proxy "FastProxy/2.1" (they said).

ingrid: curious — are we sure it's SSE chunk boundary splitting JSON string? some proxies re-chunk bytes and you can split inside a quoted string. do we have raw connection dump?

maria: attaching raw server receive stream snippet from our edge: 

[EDGE RAW] (hex) 0a646174613a207b22646f6b223a20224...
[event parse]
data: {"tool_call": {
 data: "{\"name\":\"charge\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"amount\\\":100,\\\"currency\\\":\\\"USD\\\",\\\"metadata\\\":\\\"user-123""

maria: note the repeating data: lines are multiple "data:" frames, arguments string is split across frames. our parser expects to concat frames but it looks like closing quotes/brace dropped mid-reassembly.

jon: is the customer using HTTP/2 fronted by an h2->h1 adapter? Cloudflare/fast proxies commonly re-chunk. quick mitigation: ask them to disable streaming for that endpoint or use non-streaming fallback.

aj: can reproduce locally with a small Node server that writes chunked SSE fragments where the JSON string is split mid-quote. snippet to reproduce: 
```js
const http = require('http');
http.createServer((req,res)=>{
  res.writeHead(200, { 'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream' });
  res.write('data: {"tool_call":{"name":"charge","arguments":"{\"amount\":100');
  setTimeout(()=> res.write(',\"currency\":\"USD\"}'}
  ),50);
  setTimeout(()=> res.end(),200);
}).listen(9001);
```

aj: parser on client side that simply joins event.data will fail if it naively expects balanced braces inside a single event. need to join across events.

ryan: do we already have cross-chunk reassembly in runtime? I thought we buffer until end-of-tool-call marker. if not, bug.

ingrid: runtime currently treats event.data pieces as logical increments and concatenates them, but our JSON unescape path assumes the arguments string is valid JSON per-event (we unescape once per event). so if a quoted string is cut, the unescape step can corrupt it. fix: treat the tool_call.arguments as raw bytes and perform reassembly at byte level before JSON unescape. also add a safety check: count open vs close braces and quotes to decide completeness.

jon: short-term mitigation for support: tell customer to (1) disable streaming, (2) set an SDK flag stream_mode:"complete_toolcall" which will ensure tool call events are emitted only when fully closed, or (3) add a sentinel sequence at end of arguments (e.g. "\u241E") so proxies preserving bytes will still include closure.

maria: customer prefers streaming so they can show intermediate output. can we push a hotfix for more tolerant reassembly?

ingrid: I can put up a small patch: change assembler to buffer raw event.data bytes, append, and only run JSON decode when braces/quotes are balanced. fallback to per-event decode if timeout (to avoid deadlock). will add unit tests simulating chunk splits.

support-bot: ticket created TCK-5821 — escalated to eng-oncall.

ryan: please include the FastProxy request trace headers (Via, X-Forwarded-For) so we can correlate with edge rewriter logs.

maria: added headers from customer: "Via: 1.1 fastproxy, X-Fast-ID: fp-8a2" to the ticket. pinging infra for edge reassembly logs.

aj: also logging tip: include the raw bytes length per-"data:" frame. that helps to identify if chunking happens at consistent sizes (e.g., 16KB boundary).

jon: I'll add a short-term observability metric: count JSONDecodeError during streaming tool_call reassembly and include sample trimmed traces in the error page. :chart_with_upwards_trend:

maria: thanks. I'll notify the customer with the temporary workarounds and update the ticket when ingrid's patch lands. :thumbsup:
